{
  "version": "volvox-decode-row-set/v1",
  "note": [
    "The addressing contract for a B>1 decode step, read by both",
    "tests/batched_decode_vectors.test.mjs and native/tests/test_decode_row_set.c.",
    "",
    "Expectations are derived from the contract, not recorded from a run:",
    "  write_rows[b]   = paged ? page_table[b][pos/page_tokens] * page_tokens",
    "                              + pos % page_tokens",
    "                          : b * lane_stride + positions[b]",
    "  prefix_rows     = lane-major logical order, -1 for a lane's padding",
    "  keep_mask[b][j] = (j < kv_lengths[b]) && graph_mask(b, j)",
    "  tier            = write_rows consecutive and ascending ? identity : gather",
    "",
    "These cases pin down the current dense-row active-length contract: per-lane",
    "length reaches the kernel through the keep mask, so the padded key extent is the",
    "longest lane's and every shorter lane stops at its own.",
    "",
    "A position of -1 parks a lane: it holds no request, occupies a dense row so",
    "the operands keep their shape, publishes no length, and its staged output is",
    "discarded. That is what lets a slot whose request retired -- and whose pages",
    "went back to the pool -- stay in the batch without a page to write."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "one lane is the identity tier",
      "lanes": 1,
      "positions": [
        3
      ],
      "lane_stride": 8,
      "paged": false,
      "expect": {
        "kv_lengths": [
          4
        ],
        "key_capacity": 4,
        "write_rows": [
          3
        ],
        "tier": "identity",
        "prefix_rows": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3
        ],
        "keep_mask": [
          1,
          1,
          1,
          1
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "two lanes at the same position are still strided apart",
      "lanes": 2,
      "positions": [
        2,
        2
      ],
      "lane_stride": 8,
      "paged": false,
      "expect": {
        "kv_lengths": [
          3,
          3
        ],
        "key_capacity": 3,
        "write_rows": [
          2,
          10
        ],
        "tier": "gather",
        "prefix_rows": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          8,
          9,
          10
        ],
        "keep_mask": [
          1,
          1,
          1,
          1,
          1,
          1
        ]
      }
